   $q$Kofi can afford car payments of 300 dollars per month for 24 months. At 0.5% interest per month, the most Kofi can borrow is $\sum_{k=1}^{24} \frac{300}{1.005^k}$. To the nearest cent, what is this amount?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$6768.86$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$6387.74$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"discounted-every-payment-fully"},{"text":"$7200.00$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-interest"},{"text":"$7629.59$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"computed-future-value"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$6768.86$$q$, $q$The terms form a geometric series with $a_1 = \frac{300}{1.005}$ and $r = \frac{1}{1.005}$, which simplifies to $300 \cdot \frac{1 - 1.005^{-24}}{0.005} \approx 6768.86$ dollars. The choice $7629.59$ grows the payments forward with $1.005^{24}$ instead of discounting them back to today.$q$, 'draft', null)
